  (text "EEPROM (replaces AT24C256 module)\nU501 is a swappable chip in a DIP-8 socket (only the socket is assembled): the user inserts an AT24C256 DIP-8,\ne.g. LCSC C434602 AT24C256N or C411624 24LC256-I/P.\nI2C address 0x50 (A0 = A1 = A2 = GND). The firmware layout is fixed at 32 KB (EepromLayout.h), so fit a 24C256 or 24C512.\nWP: R501 10k pulls EE_WP low (writes enabled); a jumper on J501 ties WP to +3V3 and write-protects the chip.\nNo I2C pull-ups here (they are on esp32-core)."
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "dadfeb3f-c03f-4803-acfd-31f4b1329be2")
  )
